test: give the long scenarios a window the CI runner can finish in

Run #19 (69fa178) put the CI story in focus: the first twenty scenarios
now pass - the readiness fix from 6c5d46b did its job - and exactly four
fail, all of them the ones with a long workload:

    FAIL [shpipe] missing: "exec: child 1 exit_code=0"
    FAIL [evict]  missing: "evicttest: 2 children survived to their own timeout"
    FAIL [oom]    missing: "PAGE FAULT: out of memory for pid="
    FAIL [swap]   missing: "swaptest: PASS (3 children, data intact across swap)"

In every case it is the *last* assertion of its scenario: the earlier
ones passed, so the kernel did the work and the run was then cut off.
These are the memory-pressure cases (4MB, hundreds of page faults and
disk I/O) plus the Ring3 pipeline case, and a GitHub runner is several
times slower than the machine they were tuned on.

So the windows grow rather than the workloads shrink - the workloads are
already the minimum that still creates the pressure under test:

    shpipe  20s (default) -> 60s
    evict   45s -> 150s
    oom     90s -> 180s
    swap    90s -> 180s

That is about six minutes more for a full run, which the 30 minute job
budget covers, and the settle loop still ends early once a scenario is
really finished (the window is a floor on how long the VM stays alive,
not a fixed delay).
